# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules. There are none today; this file documents
# why.
#
# The apex redirect (carta-europetravel.com to www, 308, path and query kept)
# is a zone Redirect Rule named "apex to www" in the Cloudflare dashboard, not
# a line here. Pages only matches paths in _redirects, so the domain-level line
# this file used to carry was ignored on Pages and the apex served the site
# with 200 until the rule was added (T293). Keep the apex on www: the canonical
# link and og:url in index.html both declare www, and two live hostnames would
# duplicate every crawled URL.
#
# There is deliberately no SPA catch-all (`/* /index.html 200`) here.
#
# The app is one client-rendered URL: every route lives in the hash or the query
# string, and src only ever reads window.location.pathname and writes it back
# unchanged. Nothing needs a rewrite. Note that Pages behaves as if there were a
# catch-all anyway: with no top-level 404.html in the deploy, it answers every
# unknown path with index.html and status 200. The data shards live on R2,
# which does answer 404, so a missing shard still fails loudly; the files the
# app host still serves (boot.json and the three catalogue files) do not.
# Restoring a real 404 on the app host is register row T294-a.
